---
globs: src/lib/training/**
alwaysApply: false
---

- No magic numbers. Every zone %, offset, duration, threshold lives in `src/lib/training/constants.ts` as a named `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` constant with a comment `// SOURCE: <author/title, URL>` taken from PLAN.md §7–8. If there is no source, write `// SOURCE: project default, tune` — never invent a citation or a "research says" number.
- Keep functions small and pure (input → output, no side effects). Prefer returning `{ ok: true, value } | { ok: false, error }` over throwing for invalid athlete input.
- Tests: Vitest, co-located as `<name>.test.ts`. TDD: tests are written and committed BEFORE the implementation; never edit a committed test to make it pass — ask first.
- Test the invariants in PLAN.md §7.5 and the worked examples in §9 (e.g. CSS 360 s / 180 s → 90 s/100 m; §4 splits total 5:57:00).
- Run-pace zones are % of threshold PACE (higher % = slower). Power zones are % of FTP (higher % = harder). Don't mix them up.
- Heat adjustment above 25 °C WBGT must return a warning flag (outside Ely et al. 2007 studied range).
- Discipline status: if a sport is `skill` (see `disciplineStatus`), its sessions use skill checkpoints + RPE/time targets from `skills.ts` — never zone targets. A `null` threshold means "test needed", never a guessed default.
- Equipment gating: `hasBike: false` → only indoor spin/stationary-bike "bridge" sessions; no outdoor rides, no FTP test. Open-water swim sessions always carry the safety checklist and are never solo.
- Thresholds estimated from race results (VDOT) are flagged `estimated: true` until a field test replaces them.
- The generator ALWAYS returns `{ plan, warnings[] }`. Availability (rest days, per-day `maxMinutes`, per-sport max, total sessions) and strength spacing are hard constraints; anything dropped or shortened must appear in `warnings[]` with a typed code (PLAN.md §8.9). Never throw or silently drop.
- Estimators return `{ value, method, sourceUrl, confidence, inputIds, estimated }`; zones are always derived from `bestEstimate()`, never from raw inputs.
- Athlete-specific values (Wisnu/Da Nang) live only in `seed/` and test fixtures — never hard-code them in `src/`.
- Anything that changes an existing plan (`adapt`, `easeBackIn`, modes, missed-session handling) returns `{ plan, warnings[], changes[] }`; every changed session has a `reasonCode` (PLAN.md §8.7). No silent changes, and changes must be reversible from the stored previous state (undo).
